{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>My eye has looked</b> — it is a form like וְסוּרִי in the earth (Habakkuk 3:9); it is written from the same root as שׁוֹרְרִי." "The sense of וַתַּבֵּט — that he saw with his eyes vengeance against his wicked enemies who are present with him, and likewise his ear heard concerning enemies who are not present." "And because he mentioned those who rise against me — he explained that they are doers of evil, and the bet serves in the sense of 'because of,' as if it were written בְּמֵרֵעִים."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 92, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:04.968299142Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}